What:           /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_colortemp_input
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
                Firmware-computed light colour temperature (correlated colour
                temperature) in Kelvin, processed, on
                aop-sensors-als devices with a Redbird (VD6286) sensor.
                Fractional Kelvin are reported with micro resolution. There
                is no raw photodiode-to-CCT conversion in the host driver.
                Only the documented 122-byte fake-HID report is decoded.
                Before a valid positive finite CCT arrives, reading returns
                ENODATA. A report in another layout or without a valid CCT
                leaves the last valid reading in place, independently of lux.
                CT720 and CT817 devices do not expose this attribute.
